35,2,1,talk,Midori,,"The support records are troubling. Four suppliers, two days of silence. And the warehouse rules drifted twice. The plan never held.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The calendar shows no freeze window in winter. The 2021 trial failed because the yard devices were too old. We need hardware compatibility.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, the dispatch tool skipped three upgrades. It’s been quietly aging on our racks since 2012. We can’t build on that rot.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@May, that aging tool explains the strain. My data shows two admins retiring, and the last rollout’s routines were dropped within weeks. We are losing the people who hold it together.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, that aging tool explains the invoice creep. My data shows bundled prices held, but add-ons climbed yearly. Capital requests were trimmed, yet operating lines passed unchallenged.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, that unchallenged operating spend is exactly the drift I saw. @Misaki, losing those admins means we have no one to catch the next outage.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, the silence during outages is a physical risk. If the system fails, the yard stops. We need a vendor with proven uptime, not just a contract.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, that confirms my fear. We let the system rot while approving the bills. We need a vendor who actually maintains the core, not just sells add-ons.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Midori, exactly. The eleven-month hiring gap means we cannot replace them quickly. We need a vendor who trains our people, not just installs software.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, the hiring gap is a cost center. @May, the rot is a liability. I need a vendor whose operating line stays flat, not one that grows every year.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, I agree. A single point of contact is essential. We cannot afford another two-day silence. @May, the aging tool confirms the need for a modern, stable core.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, the rot is real. But the yard devices are the immediate bottleneck. We need a vendor who supports our specific hardware mix, not just the software.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, hardware is vital, but if the core software is a decade old, no device saves us. We need a vendor who fixes the foundation, not just patches the surface.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Ryuji, hardware matters, but if the people cannot use it, it fails. I need a vendor who respects the supervisors' existing routines, not one that forces a reset.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, hardware is a capital trap. @May, the core rot is a recurring tax. I need a vendor whose total cost of ownership is predictable, not a subscription that inflates annually.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I am ready to see the candidates. We need a vendor who owns the whole picture, not just a piece of it.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I am ready. The system must survive the yard as it is, not as we wish it to be.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"I am ready. We need a partner who actually maintains the core, not one who just sells us more add-ons to patch the rot.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I am ready. The system must fit the people we have, not the ones we wish we could hire.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I am ready. The invoice trail is clear. I need a vendor whose price tag does not grow a new limb every fiscal year.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
